      "code": "dict_flags = TranslateWord2(tr, word, &words[ix], words[ix].pre_pause);",
      "note": "For the staged witness this call happens only after decoded characters have been copied out of `p_decoder` and tokenized into `sbuf`/`words[]`; unsupported punctuation is split at word boundaries, so the `word` argument here is an attacker-controlled token selected from `words[ix]`, not simply all bytes after the leading separator. That selected word is the one whose first translation emits `phonSWITCH` and whose retranslation later reaches `LookupLetter()`.",
